<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:40:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>Peltola defeats Sullivan in Alaska Senate race, expanding Democratic majority</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-peltola-defeats-sullivan-in-alaska-senate-race-expanding-democratic-majority</link><description>
Democrat Mary Peltola defeated Republican Sen. Dan Sullivan in Alaska on Tuesday, completing a political comeback in a state that US President Donald Trump has repeatedly won by wide margins. Her victory gives Democrats a 56-44 Senate majority, marking their biggest net gain in Senate seats since 1958.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90f6b112-e301-11f1-8d0c-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26308242860566.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90f6b112-e301-11f1-8d0c-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26308242860566.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8078328-e302-11f1-bcd1-89b1c3e12637</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:47:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90f6b112-e301-11f1-8d0c-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26308242860566.jpg">© Lindsey Wasson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Haitians rally behind Bukele as Salvadoran troops battle gangs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-haitians-rally-behind-bukele-as-salvadoran-troops-battle-gangs</link><description>
Thousands of Haitians took to the streets on Tuesday to urge El Salvador's President Nayib Bukele to keep fighting gangs, as his troops bolster security forces in the Caribbean nation. But experts warn that growing public support could turn to anger without a long-term plan to tackle violence and strengthen Haiti's police.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f68d9ac-e2f4-11f1-88c9-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321814589361.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f68d9ac-e2f4-11f1-88c9-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321814589361.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ae0d662c-e2f9-11f1-8226-416c2be2f9e9</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:42:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f68d9ac-e2f4-11f1-88c9-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321814589361.jpg">© Patrice Noel, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US, Mexico and Bolivia lose measles-free status as deaths mount</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-us-mexico-and-bolivia-lose-measles-free-status-as-deaths-mount</link><description>
The US has lost its measles-free status, international health officials said Tuesday, as the highly contagious virus has spread at the fastest rate in more than 30 years, while Mexico and Bolivia also lost their measles-elimination status. Vaccination rates have been falling against a number of diseases, in the US and globally, and measles has been spreading throughout the Americas since 2024. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74a1392a-3f8b-11f1-af77-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26096555305099.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74a1392a-3f8b-11f1-af77-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26096555305099.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">063e6766-e2c7-11f1-8354-17ec0c56b16d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:30:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74a1392a-3f8b-11f1-af77-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26096555305099.jpg">© Mary Conlon, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Nvidia's Jensen Huang: Targeted by the AI misinformation he helped create</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261117-deepfakes-memes-and-misinformation-ai-turns-against-nvidia-s-jensen-huang</link><description>
Nvidia co-founder Jensen Huang has become the target of a wave of AI-generated misinformation, in a striking twist for one of the men behind the AI revolution. From a fake audio recording supposedly featuring his wife to fabricated LinkedIn profiles, false claims linking him to the Chinese Communist Party and viral AI memes, Vedika Bahl examines how deepfakes and misinformation are turning against the former tech boss in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5eb9f6-e2c5-11f1-b78e-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/nvidia-3.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5eb9f6-e2c5-11f1-b78e-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/nvidia-3.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c6df240-e2c7-11f1-97d8-ef0917dcb04a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:40:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran 'playing mind games with the United States', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-playing-mind-games-with-the-united-states-expert-says</link><description>
President Donald Trump said Tuesday that US authorities take "very seriously" any possible threat to Washington, following reports Iran was planning to target officials, possibly with a radioactive bomb. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Stimson Center in Washington, says that Iran may be "playing mind games with the United States as a way perhaps of deterring President Trump from unleashing a massive new attack on Iran".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a63cda5c-e2c4-11f1-8f15-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-210522-211625-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a63cda5c-e2c4-11f1-8f15-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-210522-211625-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ab61c7c2-e2c4-11f1-a13a-459c8b2af72b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:28:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump says he takes possible Iran bomb threat to Washington 'very seriously'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-trump-says-he-takes-possible-iran-bomb-threat-to-washington-very-seriously</link><description>
President Donald Trump said Tuesday that US authorities take any possible threats to Washington ‘very seriously’, following reports that Iran was planning to target senior Trump administration officials, possibly with a radioactive bomb.  Tehran dismissed the reports as ‘fabricated’.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33aa0a04-e298-11f1-ba28-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321504671499.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33aa0a04-e298-11f1-ba28-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321504671499.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">44b532ae-e29a-11f1-9632-a7bb1405c60d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:44:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33aa0a04-e298-11f1-ba28-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321504671499.jpg">©  Aaron Favila, Pool AP via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Chase outage disrupts US online banking, Zelle payments</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-chase-outage-disrupts-online-banking-and-zelle-payments-in-united-states-us-software</link><description>
Users of several major US banking apps and online portals reported outages on Monday, according to the monitoring site Downdetector.com, with one institution ruling out a cyberattack as the cause. Among those affected by the outages were Bank of America, JPMorgan Chase and the popular money transfer app Zelle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b34ad5e-e20c-11f1-ace7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26320767161907.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b34ad5e-e20c-11f1-ace7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26320767161907.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">563385e6-e20c-11f1-b3d8-f1918d93fb3e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:40:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b34ad5e-e20c-11f1-ace7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26320767161907.jpg">© LM Otero, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump says he needs funding for air traffic control after ground stop</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-says-he-needs-funding-for-air-traffic-control-after-ground-stop</link><description>
US ​President ​Donald Trump, pressed on a ​technology ‌failure ⁠that ‌grounded thousands of ⁠flights last week, ​on ‌Monday told reporters ‌that ​the government needed funding for upgrade ​to ​air traffic ​control equipment. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Sheldon Jacobson, Professor of Computer Science at the University of Illinois. He explains that "the Republicans have had full control of the House and the Senate since the President came in. They controlled everything. If they needed the money and wanted the money they could have approved the money. The fact that they didn't, in the the different bills that have been passed, suggests that it's more than just money that is going on here".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a84d7300-e1fd-11f1-b1a8-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261116-210837-211856-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a84d7300-e1fd-11f1-b1a8-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261116-210837-211856-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">add9a8a2-e1fd-11f1-bfc5-2513a998c55a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:01:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US judge strikes down Trump visa restrictions on foreign students, journalists</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-us-judge-strikes-down-trump-visa-restrictions-on-foreign-students-journalists</link><description>
A US federal judge struck down a Trump administration policy on Monday that would have sharply limited the length of time foreign students and journalists could stay in the country, ruling that the proposed restrictions were unlawful and would undermine educational opportunity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f292a3e4-e203-11f1-abf6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/8ae939012046ee76762d8ea8784d4673a57d1b91.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f292a3e4-e203-11f1-abf6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/8ae939012046ee76762d8ea8784d4673a57d1b91.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f41b3406-e203-11f1-8b7e-47cbb88362b2</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:23:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f292a3e4-e203-11f1-abf6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/8ae939012046ee76762d8ea8784d4673a57d1b91.jpg">© Saul Loeb, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>November 17 blackout hoax: How a conspiracy theory went viral around the world</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261116-november-17-blackout-hoax-how-a-conspiracy-theory-went-viral-around-the-world</link><description>
A conspiracy theory claiming a worldwide "blackout" will hit the world on November 17 has spread across social media, with the claim it will cut electricity, internet and banking services. The rumour stems from a routine US FEMA emergency alert test, but was amplified by cryptocurrency accounts, misleading claims about EU preparedness advice and references to "The Simpsons". Recent technology outages, flight disruptions and cyberattacks have added to public anxiety, helping turn a routine test into a global hoax. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ad0d512-e1ff-11f1-9244-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/blackout.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ad0d512-e1ff-11f1-9244-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/blackout.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5e88eb3a-e1ff-11f1-8f69-45b5e3a11287</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:50:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope concludes South America homecoming, reassures faithful after cancer scare</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-pope-concludes-south-america-homecoming-reassures-faithful-after-cancer-scare</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV finished Monday his 12-day tour of Uruguay, Argentina and Peru reiterating his advocacy for social justice, environmental protection and the importance of community. Just a month after undergoing lung cancer surgery, the 71-year-old pontiff drew millions of faithful across South America, where he spent nearly two decades as a missionary.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/188735cc-e1fc-11f1-bd41-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7N43WG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/188735cc-e1fc-11f1-bd41-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7N43WG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a242b2a6-e1fb-11f1-bb50-fd482952d7fa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:50:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/188735cc-e1fc-11f1-bd41-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7N43WG.jpg">© Simone Risoluti, Vatican Media, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>The new faces of the US Congress</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/the-new-faces-of-the-us-congress</link><description>
The United States Congress is about to welcome dozens of new faces. A majority of them, Democratic, after the "blue wave" in the midterm elections. FRANCE 24's Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson catches up with one of these new lawmakers as they go through orientation as they prepare to take office in January. He speaks with Katy Padilla Stout, U.S. Representative-elect for Texas's 23rd congressional district.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95221bea-e1f9-11f1-b50f-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0c256503.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95221bea-e1f9-11f1-b50f-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0c256503.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d2b52cfa-e1f8-11f1-a1e0-011942cbe1cd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:36:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Mexican drug trade 'boss of bosses' Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo dies at 80</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-miguel-angel-felix-gallardo-mexican-drug-lord-dies</link><description>
Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo, a founder of Mexico’s Guadalajara drug cartel known as the “boss of bosses”, died in hospital on Sunday aged 80 after suffering multiple organ failure, Jalisco state’s security ministry said. Imprisoned since 1989, he had been transferred from prison to the hospital two days before his death. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7fa30ac-e142-11f1-a70a-f7625ce3d617</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:48:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA['Record number of women elected' to US Congress & governorships in midterm elections]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-record-number-of-women-elected-to-us-congress-governorships-across-country-in-midterm-elections</link><description>
Following the 2026 US midterm elections, Gavin Lee welcomes Politico Senior National Politics Reporter Lauren Fedor to discuss the growing number of Democratic women elected to Congress and governorships, particularly mothers of young children.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54cc366a-e10a-11f1-a9f0-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d8402e1a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54cc366a-e10a-11f1-a9f0-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d8402e1a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e754c538-e10a-11f1-85eb-35697e667a6f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:40:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Jensen Huang: The French Connection</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection</link><description>
President Trump is heading to Asia in a few days' time, where he is due to meet President Putin and President Xi. But there could be one fewer tech giant at the table: Jensen Huang, who has resigned from Nvidia amid a suspected espionage affair.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb9bfd36-e05e-11f1-85e3-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/Jensen-Huang-000-36PC88T.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb9bfd36-e05e-11f1-85e3-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/Jensen-Huang-000-36PC88T.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fad9359a-e05f-11f1-8600-8534dcd91768</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:03:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US probes nationwide flights stoppage as travel disruptions persist</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist</link><description>
US air travel is expected to return to normal this Sunday, following a nationwide ground stop Friday night that stranded hundreds of thousands of passengers and disrupted travel worldwide. The Trump administration blamed the incident on a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines and said there was no evidence this was a cyberattack. The ground stop now raises questions about the country's aging infrastructure and lawmakers are calling for an investigation. Analysis by Philip Mann, aviation expert at Vector Strategic Consulting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f68e5f6c-e0fd-11f1-91ae-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154335Z-516903887-RC2ONOAT735S-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f68e5f6c-e0fd-11f1-91ae-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154335Z-516903887-RC2ONOAT735S-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4dfc6f98-e0fc-11f1-bdc8-ebeb331f4797</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:09:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Air travel issues persist in the US after nationwide ground stop</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/air-travel-issues-persist-in-the-us-after-nationwide-ground-stop</link><description>
After almost five hours of grounded flights in the US, flights have resumed. However, passengers are still waiting and wading through tough logistics to get to their destinations after massive delays and cancelled flights. Details by Simon Moritz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae37617a-e0ec-11f1-9eb5-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-080531-080704-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae37617a-e0ec-11f1-9eb5-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-080531-080704-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b3965cd4-e0ec-11f1-abdc-0765d31dc03f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:12:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope laments poverty-stricken Inca communities as locals leave Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-laments-poverty-stricken-inca-communities-as-locals-leave-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV on Sunday will traverse the length of Peru in what marks the penultimate day of his Latin American tour. The leader of the Catholic church – who underwent cancer surgery just a month ago – warned that Peru's remote Inca communities are under threat as poverty continues to drive locals out of their homeland in search of better futures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16926fb2-e0e8-11f1-b2bb-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T225151Z-1773168410-RC2XNOAB3YQ0-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16926fb2-e0e8-11f1-b2bb-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T225151Z-1773168410-RC2XNOAB3YQ0-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8ccf0eaa-e0df-11f1-80f5-13c9a032c2ab</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:55:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16926fb2-e0e8-11f1-b2bb-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T225151Z-1773168410-RC2XNOAB3YQ0-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>SpaceX makes rocketry history by recapturing massive reusable rocketship</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spacex-makes-rocketry-history-by-recapturing-massive-reusable-rocketship</link><description>
After failing to catch a booster yesterday, SpaceX managed to recapture its massive reusable rocketship, "Starship" for the first time. Smaller previous models have successfully relanded but they require heavy legs and aren't fully reusable. Story by Daniel Quinlan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c43ae00-e080-11f1-8286-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T213803Z-704233441-RC2XNOAR9QE8-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEX-STARSHIP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c43ae00-e080-11f1-8286-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T213803Z-704233441-RC2XNOAR9QE8-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEX-STARSHIP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">850a30bc-e0d7-11f1-ae22-9bc5bd8b1533</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:42:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo urges stop to Amazon deforestation, demands justice for slain Indigenous leaders</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-leo-visits-peru-s-high-altitude-cusco-testing-recovery-from-lung-cancer</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV travelled across Peru on Sunday to visit communities high in the Andes mountains and deep in the Amazon rainforest, testing his recovery from lung cancer surgery a month ago. The pontiff condemned the exploitation of the Amazon and urged Catholics to oppose "with perseverance" the deforestation and pollution caused by gold and oil production in the world's largest rainforest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e3b2996-e137-11f1-9631-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T204810Z-1388210058-RC2KOOA0UH9W-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e3b2996-e137-11f1-9631-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T204810Z-1388210058-RC2KOOA0UH9W-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">970a2b7e-e0b8-11f1-a6b0-a95900a5fd00</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:51:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e3b2996-e137-11f1-9631-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T204810Z-1388210058-RC2KOOA0UH9W-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Elon Musk's SpaceX aborts booster recovery due to technical issues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/elon-musk-s-spacex-aborts-booster-recovery-due-to-technical-issues</link><description>
Elon Musk's SpaceX is in the midst of a 15th test-flight of its Starship rocket. The company was hoping to pull off the first-ever "double catch" - with both the booster and the ship itself coming safely back down to earth. Instead, an unspecified problem forced the company to abort recovery of the booster, which was diverted from its return path and crashed down into the Gulf of Mexico. Analysis by journalist Frédéric Castel, based in Bosa Chica, Texas, USA.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ecebe06-e02b-11f1-b834-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-080810-081151-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ecebe06-e02b-11f1-b834-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-080810-081151-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13e4d9b6-e02b-11f1-b702-954c0a5a64e9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:33:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Washington divided over how to deal with fallout from the Nvidia case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/washington-divided-over-how-to-deal-with-fallout-from-the-nvidia-case</link><description>
After the fall, the fallout. US government agencies are squabbling after AI leader Jensen Huang stepped down from chips giant Nvidia in disgrace. The Treasury says it wanted to blacklist a Singapore company at the heart of the scandal, but the Commerce Department didn't act. Megaspeed was run by suspected Chinese spy Alice Huang, who reportedly had an affair with Jensen Huang. Details by Peter O'Brien.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de9eb5ba-e025-11f1-b03b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120954-121129-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de9eb5ba-e025-11f1-b03b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120954-121129-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3d9bc8c-e025-11f1-88eb-81d27dcb09cf</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:21:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US: What exactly caused the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-what-exactly-caused-the-longest-nationwide-ground-stop-in-25-years</link><description>
After a nearly five-hour ground stoppage, flights in the US have resumed. However, officials are warning that it will take days to recover from the ongoing delays related to the incident. Transport Secretary Sean Duffy explained the crisis was due to a failure in ageing telecommunications equipment. What exactly happened? Answers with FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Shirli Sitbon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24754d74-e049-11f1-92be-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154753Z-749061195-RC2ONOA67Q43-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24754d74-e049-11f1-92be-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154753Z-749061195-RC2ONOA67Q43-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b0d548-e043-11f1-9d13-0df17d5d03d9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:35:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Transport Secretary asks Congress for $30 billion to upgrade aviation infrastructure</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-transport-secretary-asks-congress-for-30-bn-to-upgrade-aviation-infrastructure</link><description>
A failure in aging telecommunications equipment Friday forced a nationwide halt to departures from US airports. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin says officials have found no evidence so far of a cyberattack, but that they're not ruling it out. Details by Jack Pownall.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc695742-e040-11f1-8c71-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-150457-150644-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc695742-e040-11f1-8c71-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-150457-150644-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">017d46a8-e041-11f1-b225-ad670de86b0f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:32:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Copper wires blamed for US travel chaos as Trump asks Congress for money to overhaul system</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-copper-wires-to-blame-for-us-flight-disruption-says-trump-administration</link><description>
The Trump administration on Sunday pointed to aging infrastructure – specifically "a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines" – as being responsible for the nationwide ground stop that snarled airline travel over the weekend. The president himself blamed the administration of his predecessor Joe Biden, in his first comments on the issue after a two-day silence.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77c62198-e0bb-11f1-bcbc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304620129.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77c62198-e0bb-11f1-bcbc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304620129.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">022e82f6-e041-11f1-b63f-df8f9f615923</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:35:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77c62198-e0bb-11f1-bcbc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304620129.jpg">© Ryan Murphy, Getty Images via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>USA: All passengers survive after tanker hits docked river cruise ship in New Orleans</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans</link><description>
A portion of the Mississippi River remains closed after a collision between an oil tanker and a riverboat forced a chaotic river rescue in Louisiana. Story by Caitlin Brown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/655a8158-e024-11f1-8b4c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120344-120524-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/655a8158-e024-11f1-8b4c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120344-120524-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a3a881c-e024-11f1-8dfc-13f9b3b00dd2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:15:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world</link><description>
From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/764618c8-e025-11f1-878e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4ac3443.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/764618c8-e025-11f1-878e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4ac3443.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">405d92aa-e01f-11f1-9579-21782230ef7c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:19:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Half a million people gather for an open-air mass by Pope Leo in Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo said it was a "joy to be back" in his second home of Chiclayo, where he made his name as a bishop. This is the latest stop on his South America tour, the very tour that saw fears of cancellation after the Pope underwent surgery for lung cancer. Story by Vedika Bahl.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4004e80-e01c-11f1-be8e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T214746Z-754212400-RC29NOA0KQRS-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4004e80-e01c-11f1-be8e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T214746Z-754212400-RC29NOA0KQRS-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">81c01db6-e01b-11f1-9964-ef92d80b1580</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:17:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US nationwide flight ground stop: "Our routers got overloaded with data"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data</link><description>
On Friday, the Federal Aviation Administration issued a rare nationwide ground stop. More than 8,200 flights, or over 31% of those scheduled in the United States, were canceled. The ground stop lasted nearly five hours and was the longest in the country since September 11, 2001. Officials blamed outdated air traffic communications equipment, and said that there was no evidence of a cyber attack. The airspace is now reopened and flights have resumed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3b36d9c-e011-11f1-b125-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100114-100358-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3b36d9c-e011-11f1-b125-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100114-100358-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8cfa494-e011-11f1-8d16-95a3d2c4d031</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:14:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US flights resume after nationwide ground stop lifted</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation</link><description>
The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said that US airspace was now "opened up," and blamed "old hardware" for the travel chaos. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de33210e-dfd2-11f1-8675-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317844187470.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de33210e-dfd2-11f1-8675-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317844187470.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a751d60-dfd4-11f1-94d0-4d5742533b4a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:35:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de33210e-dfd2-11f1-8675-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317844187470.jpg">© Tony Gutierrez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
